  "same_week28_band": [
   0.9113409214582952,
   0.9137224525071085
  ],
  "verdict": "DELETION IS ONLY A CAP-CONTRIBUTION WHERE IT REMOVES A TAIL. In the 9 events where the post window survives the deletion (10% loss threshold), the cap's own contribution is -0.082 pp = 0.74% of the SAME-UNIT re-dating null width (11.10 pp). In middleearth/nucleus/abraxas the deletion removes 63.8-67.5% of the post window, so their -3.18 / +8.21 / -6.42 pp are support destruction and are NOT a cap effect; those events are excluded from the bound and must not be quoted per event. All-events pooled move (printed, not used): -0.178 pp.",
